  "member_id": "olsson-eva",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B017",
        "laureates": [
          "Harald Rose",
          "Maximilian Haider",
          "Knut Urban"
        ],
        "citation": "for spherical-aberration correction that made electron microscopy an atomic-scale quantitative instrument"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B003",
    "B015"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B017 remains a completed, experimentally verified invention that removed a fundamental electron-optical limitation and made atomic-scale quantitative imaging and spectroscopy reproducible in independent laboratories. This is an enduring change in what can be observed and measured across materials physics, not recognition for subsequent scientific applications alone. The proposed trio still offers the most plausible compact line from Rose's decisive corrector concepts to successful realization and validation by Haider and Urban.",
    "case_against": "The credit history remains the principal reservation. Corrector theory, engineering, early demonstrations, commercial implementation, and later refinement involved a wider chain of contributors, so the committee must establish that these three names identify the original decisive stages rather than merely prominent later development. If that archival reconstruction fails, the achievement should not be forced into an arbitrary allocation.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll favors B003 because optical lattice clocks combine a sharply defined physical principle, reproducible exceptional performance, broad metrological uptake, and a compact Katori-Ye attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B003 is the strongest alternative and that its two-person attribution presently appears cleaner. It also reinforces the importance of an instrument that delivers independently reproducible measurement. I retain B017 because aberration correction has already made a broad and durable observational capability routine across materials research; the relevant question is whether our historical review can confirm its exact original credit, not whether its experimental transformation is mature."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B017 as a transformative established quantitative probe but cautions that its credit spans theoretical design, instrument engineering, and multiple implementation teams.",
        "response": "I agree fully with the caution. The breadth of the development chain is precisely why the citation must be confined to spherical-aberration correction and why Rose, Haider, and Urban require role-by-role priority review. On the present record, that complexity does not diminish the singularity of the invention or its independently demonstrated consequences; it defines the evidentiary standard for final attribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that B009's quantum-error-correction principles are mature despite the lack of scalable fault-tolerant computation, citing logical-qubit demonstrations.",
        "response": "The logical-qubit evidence makes B009 more compelling than a merely prospective programme. Nevertheless, its proposed citation combines codes, fault tolerance, and topological protection, and the historical unity and completeness of the three-person allocation remain unresolved. B017 offers a more directly bounded experimental invention whose physical capability has long been visible, tested, and widely used."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival and expert review can demonstrate that Rose, Haider, and Urban are the uniquely defensible allocation across original corrector theory, first successful implementation, and validation.",
      "Where to draw the boundary between the credited invention of correction and later engineering, commercial implementation, and refinements.",
      "Whether B003's cleaner attribution should prevail if the B017 historical record proves unable to support this precise three-person allocation."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
